The bisection method finds a root of \(f(x)=0\) by repeatedly halving an interval \([a_n,b_n]\) that brackets a sign change of \(f\), keeping whichever half still brackets it:
\[
m_n=\frac{a_n+b_n}{2},\qquad
(a_{n+1},b_{n+1})=
\begin{cases}
(a_n,m_n) & f(a_n)f(m_n)&lt;0,\\[2pt]
(m_n,b_n) & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\]

// VM is the shared utility library, loaded globally via _includes/head-scripts.html (js/**). This page uses VM.sampling.seededRandom, VM.sampling.gaussianRandom, VM.plotting.paddedRange, VM.expressions.makeNumber, VM.ui.renderTable, VM.ui.applyExampleParams.
